KZ3 patch 2145 (RSX pass 134): one upscaler interface (libs/video/rsx_upscale.h) and AMD FidelityFX Super Resolution 1 behind it.

Off by default: with RSX_UPSCALE unset nothing is created, no pass or copy is recorded, the present is as before.
RSX_UPSCALE=fsr1 (RSX_UPSCALE_SHARPNESS 0..2 RCAS stops, default 0.2) upscales the 1280x720 image to the size the display
scaling rectangle has (rsx_dm_rect_for, patch 2095) with EASU + RCAS D3D12 compute passes; ld_dm_blit then copies the
result 1:1. It runs on the composed picture at present (scene and HUD are one 720p image in this game: no pre-HUD tap);
rsx_upscale_pre_hud is the tap for a game that has a separate HUD pass. Nothing in rsx_upscale* is game-specific.

Files: rsx_upscale.h/.c (backend ids NONE FSR1 DLAA DLSS FSR3 XESS, parse, quality ratios and render-size math, the
context, the NULL = off rule), rsx_upscale_fsr1.c (constants through the vendored headers' CPU mode, HLSL assembly),
rsx_upscale_d3d12.c (the two compute passes, D3DCompile cs_5_0 like the renderer's other HLSL), fsr1/ (AMD's ffx_a.h and
ffx_fsr1.h unmodified, MIT, LICENSE.txt, README.txt; fsr1_embed.h generated from them by tools/smoke/fsr1_embed.py).
FidelityFX FSR 1: https://github.com/GPUOpen-Effects/FidelityFX-FSR commit a21ffb8f6c13233ba336352bdff293894c706575,
MIT, Copyright (c) 2021 Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.
Not run under Proton or on a GPU (game data offline): host tests and the Windows compile only (tools/smoke/test_upscale.sh).
Adding files under libs/video changes the shader translator id (patch 2141): the PSO preload cache is rebuilt once.
The intermediate texture is re-made whenever it is missing or its size differs from the output size, also with a caller-provided
output (from the Killzone 2 port's patch 6052; otherwise its size goes stale after a resolution change).
Upstream candidate (the interface and FSR 1 backend are generic).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.19.0 (SPU pass 154): the include line for rsx_d3d12_device.h (patch 2099 added it; upstream has it) is not in the context any more.

